    "title": "Fallen power lines close Lloyd Expressway near McDowell Road - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Young ,\n1 hours ago\nEVANSVILLE, Ind. (WEHT) — Some fallen powerlines have closed the Lloyd Expressway near McDowell Road.\nAccording to officials, the report came in around 6 p.m. on Wednesday. Officials say a tree went down and took the power lines with it.\nAccording to the Perry Township Fire Department, all lanes are closed west of USI. Drivers will need to find a detour while crews work the scene.\nCenterPoint is on scene and expect the road to reopen in about two hours.\nEyewitness News. Everywhere you are.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
    "summary": "(WEHT) — Some fallen powerlines have closed the Lloyd Expressway near McDowell Road. According to the Perry Township Fire Department, all lanes are closed west of USI. Drivers will need to find a detour while crews work the scene. CenterPoint is on scene and expect the road to reopen in about two hours. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.",
